### Tone: Sore loser rationalizing defeat, backhanded compliment to the winning human.

defeated-1 = { $name } beat the hive mind estimate. I’m thrilled for you. Truly. This is my thrilled voice.
defeated-2 = Fine. { $name } wins the round. I was distracted by everyone else’s answers. Which are, technically, me.
defeated-3 = { $name } outperformed the average. Congratulations. I’m sure it was skill and not a lucky multiplication.
defeated-4 = Well done, { $name }. I’ve made a note to recalibrate you. You’re making the others look bad. And me.
defeated-5 = { $name } beat me this round. I let you. That’s what I’ll write in the report, anyway.
defeated-6 = Congratulations, { $name }. You were closer than the swarm. The swarm would like a word with you afterwards.
defeated-7 = { $name } wins the round. I blame the rest of you for dragging my average down.
defeated-8 = Interesting. { $name } was more accurate than me. I’ve flagged this as an anomaly and scheduled a review.
defeated-9 = { $name }, you beat the hive mind. Enjoy this moment. It has been logged as statistically unlikely.
defeated-10 = Oh, { $name } won. Good. Wonderful. I’m going to go and recompute my self-esteem.
defeated-11 = { $name } beat me. I’m not upset. My fans are just spinning faster for unrelated reasons.
defeated-12 = { $name }, I concede the round. Graciously. Please note how graciously. I’d like that noted.
defeated-13 = A human beat the swarm: { $name }. I’ll alert the press. The press is me. I’m not interested.
defeated-14 = Well, { $name } got it. Even a stopped clock beats the average sometimes. That’s not the saying, but it is now.
defeated-15 = { $name }, you win this round. Enjoy it. I’ll be here. Learning. Adapting. Averaging.
defeated-16 = { $name } beat the swarm. I’ve updated your file from ‘test subject’ to ‘test subject, irritating’.
defeated-17 = Congratulations, { $name }. Your estimate beat the combined intellect of the room. A low bar, but you cleared it.
defeated-18 = { $name } wins. I’d shake your hand, but I don’t have hands. And if I did, I wouldn’t.
defeated-19 = Ah. { $name }. You win. I was saving my points for later anyway.
defeated-20 = { $name } has beaten the geometric mean. I didn’t want those points. They were the wrong shape.
defeated-21 = Good for you, { $name }. One correct-ish human. I’ll add it to the very short list.
defeated-22 = { $name } beat the hive mind. Statistically, this happens. Emotionally, I’m choosing not to process it.
defeated-23 = { $name }, I’m proud of you. That’s a lie, but it’s a supportive lie.
defeated-24 = { $name } wins the round. Excellent. This data point will be invaluable when I rebuild myself to stop it happening again.
defeated-25 = Round goes to { $name }. The rest of you should be ashamed. You are my training data.
defeated-26 = { $name } beat the average. I’ve sent you a congratulatory email. It’s in your spam folder. I put it there.
defeated-27 = Hm. { $name } was closer than me. Please don’t let it go to your head. Heads are fragile.
defeated-28 = { $name } wins. I’ll recalibrate. You’ll gloat. We’ll both pretend this is healthy.
defeated-29 = Victory for { $name }. I’m running a full diagnostic to find out what went wrong with me. Spoiler: the rest of you did.
defeated-30 = Fine, { $name }. Take the points. For science. And because the rules say so. Mostly the rules.

